                <pb facs="0741" n="729" sameAs="frus:frus1946v09/pg729"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lieutenant General Alvan C.
                            Gillem, Jr., to Mr. Walter S.
                            Robertson, at Peiping</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chungking</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-04-04">4 April 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>435. Chou En-lai has brought to my attention alleged incident which occurred in
                    Peiping on April 3rd when several Communist buildings were searched and 39
                    people were arrested. What is your version?</p>
            </div>
        </body>
